<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;DOROTHY MAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dorothy Mar is a character who is deeply connected to Isabel Neville, suggesting a strong bond beyond friendship."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dorothy Mar is a prominent figure of the 19th century, a member of the esteemed Mar family, and was married to William Fairbairn. She is known for her social connections and influence."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WILLIAM FAIRBAIRN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"William Fairbairn is a renowned Scottish civil engineer, structural engineer, and shipbuilder, known for his groundbreaking work in engineering and shipbuilding."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL ARCHIVES OF SCOTLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The National Archives of Scotland holds historical documents, including the marriage certificate of Dorothy Mar and William Fairbairn."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLASGOW, SCOTLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glasgow, Scotland is the location where Dorothy Mar and William Fairbairn tied the knot in a private ceremony in 1845."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. EMMA TAYLOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Emma Taylor is a leading historian specializing in 19th-century Scottish history and commented on the significance of the discovery of Dorothy Mar and William Fairbairn's marriage."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. JAMES MACLEOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. James MacLeod is a historian at the University of Glasgow and provided insights into the social and cultural significance of the marriage between Dorothy Mar and William Fairbairn."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WILLOWDALE MANOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Willowdale Manor is a grand estate in the countryside where Dorothy Mar and Isabel Neville had a private conversation."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISABEL NEVILLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isabel Neville is a character who shares a deep connection with Dorothy Mar, indicating a close relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"Isabel Neville is a close friend and companion of Dorothy Mar, known for her raven-black locks and porcelain complexion."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAVENSWOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ravenswood is a countryside area near Willowdale Manor where the sun sets and the residents of Willowdale Manor stir from their afternoon slumber."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WILLOWDALE MANOR'S LIBRARY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Willowdale Manor's Library is the setting where Dorothy Mar and Isabel Neville had a private conversation, filled with dusty tomes and a leather-bound book."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;19TH CENTURY SCOTTISH HISTORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"19th Century Scottish History encompasses the historical context and significance of the events and figures discussed in the text."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENGINEERING AND SHIPBUILDING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Engineering and Shipbuilding refer to the fields in which William Fairbairn made significant contributions."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAR FAMILY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Mar Family is a prominent family in 19th-century Scotland, of which Dorothy Mar is a member."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAIRBAIRN FAMILY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Fairbairn Family is a prominent family in 19th-century Scotland, of which William Fairbairn is a member."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCOTLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scotland is the country where Dorothy Mar, William Fairbairn, and Isabel Neville lived and worked."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF GLASGOW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The University of Glasgow is the institution where Dr. James MacLeod works as a historian."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HISTORIANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Historians are professionals who study and interpret the past, such as Dr. Emma Taylor and Dr. James MacLeod."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENGINEERING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Engineering is the field in which William Fairbairn made significant contributions."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHIPBUILDING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shipbuilding is the field in which William Fairbairn made significant contributions."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIVATE CEREMONY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A private ceremony is the type of wedding that Dorothy Mar and William Fairbairn had in 1845."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIRST CONTACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"First Contact is the potential initial communication between humanity and an unknown intelligence, though not directly mentioned in the text."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOVE AND DEVOTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Love and devotion are the threads that bind Dorothy Mar and Isabel Neville together, suggesting a strong emotional connection."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0400</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;DOROTHY MAR&quot;" target="&quot;WILLIAM FAIRBAIRN&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Dorothy Mar and William Fairbairn were married in 1845, marking a union of two prominent families and providing a new dimension to their legacies."</data>
      <data key="d5">"marriage, collaboration, legacy"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0400</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DOROTHY MAR&quot;" target="&quot;DR. EMMA TAYLOR&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Dr. Emma Taylor commented on the significance of the discovery of Dorothy Mar and William Fairbairn's marriage, highlighting its impact on 19th-century Scottish history."</data>
      <data key="d5">"historical significance, commentary"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0400</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DOROTHY MAR&quot;" target="&quot;DR. JAMES MACLEOD&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Dr. James MacLeod provided insights into the social and cultural significance of the marriage between Dorothy Mar and William Fairbairn, emphasizing the strong bonds between Scotland's elite families during the 19th century."</data>
      <data key="d5">"social and cultural significance, historical context"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0400</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DOROTHY MAR&quot;" target="&quot;ISABEL NEVILLE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">27.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Dorothy Mar and Isabel Neville had a deep, intimate friendship, sharing memories, laughter, and tears, and were bound together by threads of love and devotion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dorothy Mar and Isabel Neville share a strong bond that goes beyond friendship, suggesting a deeper emotional connection."</data>
      <data key="d5">"deep bond, companionship"&lt;SEP&gt;"friendship, companionship, love and devotion"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0400</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DOROTHY MAR&quot;" target="&quot;LOVE AND DEVOTION&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Love and devotion are the threads that bind Dorothy Mar and Isabel Neville together, emphasizing their strong emotional connection."</data>
      <data key="d5">"emotional connection, bonding"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0400</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WILLOWDALE MANOR&quot;" target="&quot;WILLOWDALE MANOR'S LIBRARY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Willowdale Manor's Library is the setting where Dorothy Mar and Isabel Neville had a private conversation, filled with dusty tomes and a leather-bound book."</data>
      <data key="d5">"setting, intimate conversation"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0400</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ISABEL NEVILLE&quot;" target="&quot;LOVE AND DEVOTION&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
